1
00:00:18,000 --> 00:00:19,500
Okay, help me out here.

2
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:23,170
How does an archeology professor get that good with a whip?

3
00:00:23,170 --> 00:00:25,670
Maybe he took a class at the adult bookstore.

4
00:00:25,680 --> 00:00:27,340
That's how I learned.

5
00:00:27,340 --> 00:00:30,150
I can't believe you've never seen  Raiders of the Lost Ark.

6
00:00:30,150 --> 00:00:33,920
And I can't believe you've never read  Eat, Pray, Love.

7
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:35,550
When she comes out with

8
00:00:35,550 --> 00:00:38,150
Eat, Pray, Run Away From A   Giant Boulder, I'll read it.

9
00:00:40,360 --> 00:00:43,020
I don't care if Eat, Pray, Love changed your life,

10
00:00:43,030 --> 00:00:45,230
I'm not reading it.

11
00:00:46,030 --> 00:00:48,260
You know, I could totally rock a hat like that.

12
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:51,030
That's the work of noted Hollywood costume designer

13
00:00:51,030 --> 00:00:52,100
Deborah Nadoolman.

14
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:53,440
She also designed

15
00:00:53,440 --> 00:00:54,840
the iconic red and black jacket

16
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:56,640
in Michael Jackson's Thriller video,

17
00:00:56,640 --> 00:00:58,640
which I've never viewed in its entirety,

18
00:00:58,640 --> 00:01:00,080
as I find zombies dancing

19
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:02,480
in choreographed synchronicity implausible.

20
00:01:03,410 --> 00:01:06,920
And also, it's really scary.

21
00:01:06,920 --> 00:01:10,020
Would someone please turn off the Sheldon commentary track?

22
00:01:10,020 --> 00:01:13,760
There's no switch. Just listen and learn.

23
00:01:14,860 --> 00:01:16,320
Penny, if you think this is good,

24
00:01:16,330 --> 00:01:17,790
you should come with us Friday

25
00:01:17,790 --> 00:01:19,660
to see it on the big screen at the Colonial.

26
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:20,960
Well, I'm watching it now.

27
00:01:20,960 --> 00:01:22,430
Why would I want to see it again on Friday?

28
00:01:22,430 --> 00:01:24,270
Because the print they're showing on Friday

29
00:01:24,270 --> 00:01:28,270
has an additional 21 seconds of previously unseen footage.

30
00:01:28,270 --> 00:01:32,410
What? 21 seconds? That'll be like seeing a whole new movie!

31
00:01:33,210 --> 00:01:34,440
Exactly.

32
00:01:34,440 --> 00:01:36,210
They say it finally solves the submarine controversy.

33
00:01:36,210 --> 00:01:37,950
Did-- Leonard?

34
00:01:37,950 --> 00:01:39,050
I'm no expert, but I believe

35
00:01:39,050 --> 00:01:41,850
what we just heard from Penny was sarcasm.

36
00:01:42,390 --> 00:01:44,720
Oh! Good.

37
00:01:44,720 --> 00:01:46,850
I'm 8 for 26 this month.

38
00:01:47,960 --> 00:01:49,090
Yeah, I think I'll pass.

39
00:01:49,090 --> 00:01:52,030
But you guys enjoy your extra 21 seconds.

40
00:01:52,030 --> 00:01:53,460
Bet if I could make you understand

41
00:01:53,460 --> 00:01:55,730
why this is such a cool thing, we'd still be together.

42
00:01:55,730 --> 00:01:59,230
Mm, yeah, no, we wouldn't.

43
00:01:59,240 --> 00:02:00,640
Uh-huh.

44
00:02:00,640 --> 00:02:04,610
I'm guessing 21 seconds had something to do with that, too.

45
00:02:35,820 --> 00:02:37,360
May I point out to you all

46
00:02:37,360 --> 00:02:39,660
that the screening is "first come, first served"?

47
00:02:39,660 --> 00:02:43,260
Relax, it's 5:00. The movie doesn't start till midnight.

48
00:02:43,260 --> 00:02:45,630
Another way of saying that is

49
00:02:45,630 --> 00:02:47,700
"the movie starts at midnight, and it's already 5:00."

50
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:49,240
Let's go.

51
00:02:49,240 --> 00:02:51,310
You know, if we miss it, we'll have the fun of

52
00:02:51,310 --> 00:02:54,610
listening to Sheldon whine about it for the rest of our lives.

53
00:02:54,610 --> 00:02:57,440
See? Howard's on my side.

54
00:02:57,450 --> 00:02:59,150
Actually, I'm not.

55
00:02:59,150 --> 00:03:01,120
I'm using sarcasm to mock you.

56
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:04,990
Drat. Now I'm 8 for 27.

57
00:03:04,990 --> 00:03:07,020
Don't worry, Sheldon.We'll be fine.

58
00:03:07,020 --> 00:03:08,990
What happened to the Leonard Hofstadter

59
00:03:08,990 --> 00:03:11,430
who waited in line with me for 14 hours

60
00:03:11,430 --> 00:03:13,630
to see the midnight premiere of Star Trek: Nemesis?

61
00:03:13,630 --> 00:03:16,430
Oh. Well, he waited in line for 14 hours,

62
00:03:16,430 --> 00:03:18,030
while you napped in a lawn chair,

63
00:03:18,030 --> 00:03:19,700
he got in a fight with a Klingon

64
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:21,340
when he stepped out of line to pee

65
00:03:21,340 --> 00:03:23,200
and you wouldn't wake up to vouch for him,

66
00:03:23,200 --> 00:03:26,570
and worst of all, he saw Star Trek: Nemesis.

67
00:03:26,570 --> 00:03:28,710
But how were our seats?

68
00:03:28,710 --> 00:03:29,780
Excellent.

69
00:03:29,780 --> 00:03:31,380
I rest my case.

70
00:03:31,380 --> 00:03:34,820
Amy, don't you agree we should leave now and get in line?

71
00:03:36,120 --> 00:03:38,490
Actually, as the newest member of your social group,

72
00:03:38,490 --> 00:03:40,690
I believe I'll gain more acceptance by arbitrarily

73
00:03:40,690 --> 00:03:42,990
siding with your friends from time to time.

74
00:03:42,990 --> 00:03:45,990
Shrewd.

75
00:03:45,990 --> 00:03:48,600
Leonard, you're right.

76
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:50,600
We should enjoy our meal, arrive late,

77
00:03:50,600 --> 00:03:52,270
and risk winding up with terrible seats,

78
00:03:52,270 --> 00:03:54,330
assuming we get in at all.

79
00:03:54,340 --> 00:03:56,040
Thank you, Amy.

80
00:03:56,040 --> 00:03:59,640
See? It's working.

81
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:01,610
Knock-knock.

82
00:04:01,610 --> 00:04:02,740
Who's there?

83
00:04:02,740 --> 00:04:03,740
Olive.[I love u]

84
00:04:03,750 --> 00:04:06,710
Olive you, too.

85
00:04:06,710 --> 00:04:09,050
Guys, that's really starting to get old.

86
00:04:09,050 --> 00:04:10,180
Knock-knock.

87
00:04:10,190 --> 00:04:11,290
Who's there?

88
00:04:11,290 --> 00:04:14,120
I have a girlfriend and you don't.

89
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:16,190
Hysterical!

90
00:04:16,190 --> 00:04:18,430
Wait, now, we don't know that yet. He isn't finished.

91
00:04:18,430 --> 00:04:21,230
I have a girlfriend and you don't who?

92
00:04:21,230 --> 00:04:25,430
So. Are you sure you don't want to come with us to Raiders?

93
00:04:25,430 --> 00:04:28,440
Oh, no. That movie has melting faces.

94
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:30,070
It reminds me too much of the time

95
00:04:30,070 --> 00:04:32,070
I dropped that vial of flesh-eating bacteria

96
00:04:32,070 --> 00:04:33,340
into the Rhesus monkey lab.

97
00:04:36,040 --> 00:04:38,380
Besides, Penny and I are having a girls' night tonight.

98
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:40,550
Girls' night?  What does that entail?

99
00:04:40,550 --> 00:04:42,150
Oh, you know, girls get together,

100
00:04:42,150 --> 00:04:43,680
hang out, share girl talk.

101
00:04:44,690 --> 00:04:46,720
I'm a girl.

102
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:51,290
Oh. Well, maybe you can join us. I'll ask Penny.

103
00:04:51,290 --> 00:04:54,230
No need. Penny and I are very close.

104
00:04:54,230 --> 00:04:55,930
You are?

105
00:04:55,930 --> 00:04:58,470
Yes. In fact, our menses are synchronized.

106
00:05:03,870 --> 00:05:05,540
Penny.

107
00:05:05,540 --> 00:05:07,470
Bernadette tells me you're planning a girls' night.

108
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:11,410
I'm a girl.

109
00:05:11,410 --> 00:05:14,080
Oh. Um, it was -- it was just going to be me and Bernadette.

110
00:05:14,080 --> 00:05:15,950
Besides, I thought you were going to the movies

111
00:05:15,950 --> 00:05:17,020
with Sheldon and the guys.

112
00:05:17,020 --> 00:05:18,390
Yes, but they're not girls.

113
00:05:18,390 --> 00:05:20,590
I'm a girl.

114
00:05:20,590 --> 00:05:24,660
Yeah, no, no, I-I-I got that.

115
00:05:24,660 --> 00:05:26,160
What's the dress code?

116
00:05:26,160 --> 00:05:28,100
Uh, just wear something comfortable.

117
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:31,900
All right. I'll have to go shopping.

118
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:34,840
Knock-knock.

119
00:05:34,840 --> 00:05:35,940
Who is there?

120
00:05:35,940 --> 00:05:37,540
- Hugh.  - Hugh who?

121
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:40,240
Hugh people need to listen to me.

122
00:05:44,450 --> 00:05:47,850
It's time to get in line for the movie.

123
00:05:47,850 --> 00:05:50,280
And that's how you tell a knock-knock joke.

124
00:05:53,350 --> 00:05:59,130
Under normal circumstances I'd say, "I told you so".

125
00:05:59,130 --> 00:06:01,330
But as I have told you so

126
00:06:01,330 --> 00:06:03,860
with such vehemence and frequency already,

127
00:06:03,860 --> 00:06:05,930
the phrase has lost all meaning.

128
00:06:05,930 --> 00:06:08,570
Therefore, I will be replacing it with the phrase:

129
00:06:08,570 --> 00:06:10,940
"I informed you thusly".

130
00:06:10,940 --> 00:06:13,710
Ooh. Can't wait for that to start.

131
00:06:13,710 --> 00:06:16,010
I informed you thusly.

132
00:06:16,010 --> 00:06:19,510
8 for 28.

133
00:06:19,510 --> 00:06:21,410
This is where we could have been

134
00:06:21,410 --> 00:06:23,380
if we hadn't stopped for dinner.

135
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:25,550
This is where we could have been

136
00:06:25,550 --> 00:06:27,920
if Koothrappali hadn't ordered dessert.

137
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:29,990
Well I earned it, dude, I ate all my broccoli.

138
00:06:29,990 --> 00:06:35,160
And here's where we are. The runts in a large litter.

139
00:06:35,160 --> 00:06:36,830
Unlikely to ever reach

140
00:06:36,830 --> 00:06:40,870
the nourishing teats of Indiana Jones.

141
00:06:40,870 --> 00:06:43,740
So I guess it's a good thing we stopped for dinner.

142
00:06:46,070 --> 00:06:48,710
You know, guys, when facing disappointment,

143
00:06:48,710 --> 00:06:49,910
Eat, Pray, Loveteaches us --

144
00:06:49,910 --> 00:06:52,480
Oh, shut up.

145
00:06:53,880 --> 00:06:56,250
...So anyway, to make a long story short,

146
00:06:56,250 --> 00:06:59,820
turns out I have an unusually firm cervix.

147
00:07:02,060 --> 00:07:05,190
You know -- Amy, when we say "girl talk",

148
00:07:05,190 --> 00:07:09,100
it doesn't just have to be about our lady parts.

149
00:07:09,100 --> 00:07:11,980
Shame. 'Cause I have a real zinger

150
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:13,900
about my tilted uterus.

151
00:07:18,270 --> 00:07:21,110
Penny, your nails look great.

152
00:07:21,110 --> 00:07:24,280
Oh, thanks. I found this place in Alhambra.

153
00:07:24,280 --> 00:07:25,750
It's in a woman's basement.

154
00:07:25,750 --> 00:07:28,150
I think it's a front for human trafficking,

155
00:07:28,150 --> 00:07:30,020
but they do a really good job.

156
00:07:31,720 --> 00:07:34,050
A colleague of mine did her graduate thesis on the fungus

157
00:07:34,060 --> 00:07:36,820
that grows on improperly sterilized manicure implements.

158
00:07:37,830 --> 00:07:40,760
Well don't tell me that's not "girl talk".

159
00:07:40,760 --> 00:07:43,700
So where should we go tonight?

160
00:07:43,700 --> 00:07:45,900
A bar? A club? A movie?

161
00:07:45,900 --> 00:07:47,530
Or we could just stay here.

162
00:07:47,540 --> 00:07:49,140
Yes, a continue to bond.

163
00:07:49,140 --> 00:07:50,840
I have a feeling that after tonight,

164
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:53,340
one of you will become my best friend forever.

165
00:07:53,340 --> 00:07:56,380
Or "BFF," if you prefer.

166
00:07:56,380 --> 00:07:57,740
Which I don't.

167
00:07:57,750 --> 00:08:02,050
All right, time to open Bachelor Number Two.

168
00:08:02,050 --> 00:08:04,450
Gee, I don't know if I should drink more.

169
00:08:04,450 --> 00:08:06,650
I have to drive home, and I've got enough trouble

170
00:08:06,650 --> 00:08:09,390
seeing over the dashboard as it is.

171
00:08:09,390 --> 00:08:12,730
That's okay. You can just sleep here.

172
00:08:12,730 --> 00:08:15,060
Oh, good, a slumber party!

173
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:17,400
We'll do makeovers, initiate phony phone calls,

174
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:20,370
and have spirited pillow fights in our frilly nighties!

175
00:08:20,370 --> 00:08:21,900
Oh, gosh, Amy.

176
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:24,370
I don't know if I would call this an actual slumber party.

177
00:08:24,370 --> 00:08:25,910
Well, that's disappointing.

178
00:08:25,910 --> 00:08:27,510
I've always wanted to be invited to a slumber party.

179
00:08:27,510 --> 00:08:29,010
Oh, you never were?

180
00:08:29,010 --> 00:08:30,510
Not even when you were a kid?

181
00:08:30,510 --> 00:08:33,050
Well, there was the time I had my tonsils out,

182
00:08:33,050 --> 00:08:35,480
and I shared a room with a little Vietnamese girl.

183
00:08:36,850 --> 00:08:38,290
She didn't make it through the night,

184
00:08:38,290 --> 00:08:40,490
but up till then, it was kind of fun.

185
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:46,030
Okay. Well, I guess we're having a slumber party.

186
00:08:48,700 --> 00:08:51,060
Pillow fight!

187
00:08:53,940 --> 00:08:56,640
Oh, I hope they let us in soon.

188
00:08:56,640 --> 00:08:59,170
I'm tired of running to the gas station to use the bathroom.

189
00:08:59,170 --> 00:09:02,340
The guy makes me buy a Gatorade every time.

190
00:09:02,340 --> 00:09:03,780
It's a vicious circle.

191
00:09:03,780 --> 00:09:07,780
Too bad you don't have a stadium pal like me.

192
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:09,150
What's a stadium pal?

193
00:09:09,150 --> 00:09:10,780
Let me put it this way:

194
00:09:10,790 --> 00:09:12,590
takes care of the bathroom problem,

195
00:09:12,590 --> 00:09:14,120
and it keeps your calf warm.

196
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:18,660
Hey, guys, bad news. I just did a quick calculation.

197
00:09:18,660 --> 00:09:21,130
Given the size of the theater and the length of this line,

198
00:09:21,130 --> 00:09:22,830
we might not get seats.

199
00:09:23,900 --> 00:09:26,130
What did he say?

200
00:09:26,130 --> 00:09:27,370
Nice going, Raj.

201
00:09:27,370 --> 00:09:29,170
Just got him down for his nap.

202
00:09:30,670 --> 00:09:32,640
We might not get seats?!

203
00:09:32,640 --> 00:09:34,310
It's fine, it's fine.Go back to sleep.

204
00:09:34,310 --> 00:09:37,740
Oh, I informed you thusly! I so informed you thusly.

205
00:09:37,750 --> 00:09:40,450
Howard, you talk to him.

206
00:09:40,450 --> 00:09:41,750
Howard?

207
00:09:43,820 --> 00:09:45,590
You're peeing, aren't you?

208
00:09:47,420 --> 00:09:48,760
Hey, look who's here!

209
00:09:48,760 --> 00:09:50,490
Hey, buddies!

210
00:09:50,490 --> 00:09:52,090
Well, if it isn't Wil Wheaton,

211
00:09:52,090 --> 00:09:56,130
the Jar Jar Binks of the Star Trek universe.

212
00:09:56,130 --> 00:09:59,770
(la Ja Ja Binks)Mee-sa think that very funny!

213
00:09:59,770 --> 00:10:03,640
Well, you-sa can go think that at the back of the line.

214
00:10:03,640 --> 00:10:06,010
No cuts, no buts, no coconuts.

215
00:10:07,210 --> 00:10:08,680
Wil Wheaton.

216
00:10:08,680 --> 00:10:09,440
Yeah.

217
00:10:09,440 --> 00:10:10,280
I'm a big fan.

218
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:13,980
Of what? Poorly executed beards?

219
00:10:13,980 --> 00:10:15,980
Do you think you could get me and my friends into the movie?

220
00:10:15,980 --> 00:10:17,250
We got here a little late.

221
00:10:17,250 --> 00:10:19,050
No problem. Come on, I'll hook you up.

222
00:10:19,050 --> 00:10:21,490
Awesome.

223
00:10:21,490 --> 00:10:24,860
We-sa gonna go into the movie now! Bye-bye!

224
00:10:27,260 --> 00:10:29,830
This is Indiana Jones,

225
00:10:29,830 --> 00:10:31,730
not Star Trek.

226
00:10:31,730 --> 00:10:34,670
There should be no value to his pseudo-celebrity here!

227
00:10:34,670 --> 00:10:36,340
And even at Star Trek conventions,

228
00:10:36,340 --> 00:10:39,270
they only let him in if he helps set up!

229
00:10:39,270 --> 00:10:40,940
Calm down, Sheldon.

230
00:10:40,940 --> 00:10:42,440
I will not calm down.

231
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:45,450
This affront to justice and decency cannot go unanswered.

232
00:10:45,450 --> 00:10:48,210
As Captain Jean-Luc Picard once said,

233
00:10:48,220 --> 00:10:51,280
"The line must be drawn here!

234
00:10:51,290 --> 00:10:54,920
"This far, no farther!"

235
00:10:55,220 --> 00:10:58,160
Had to wake him up from his nap, didn't you?

236
00:11:02,290 --> 00:11:04,330
You know what I really love about Howard?

237
00:11:04,330 --> 00:11:06,130
His chest hair.

238
00:11:07,670 --> 00:11:09,800
Howard has a hairy chest?

239
00:11:09,800 --> 00:11:11,800
No, just the one.

240
00:11:13,140 --> 00:11:15,240
But it's really long.

241
00:11:17,280 --> 00:11:20,480
Okay, there you go-- Sultry Sunrise Red.

242
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:22,080
What do you think?

243
00:11:22,080 --> 00:11:24,820
My nails have never looked so pretty before.

244
00:11:24,820 --> 00:11:26,780
Get it off.

245
00:11:29,150 --> 00:11:31,020
Oh, oh, uh, looks like they're getting ready

246
00:11:31,020 --> 00:11:32,020
to let people in.

247
00:11:32,020 --> 00:11:35,130
Listen to what Mr. Wil Wheaton is tweeting.

248
00:11:35,130 --> 00:11:38,930
"Best seats in house for Raiders screening.

249
00:11:38,930 --> 00:11:42,100
Suck on that, Sheldon Cooper."

250
00:11:42,100 --> 00:11:43,870
Why do you read his Twitter feed?

251
00:11:43,870 --> 00:11:45,770
You know it's only going to upset you.

252
00:11:45,770 --> 00:11:48,040
I believe in knowing my enemy, Leonard.

253
00:11:48,040 --> 00:11:51,410
Had Twitter existed at the time, would not General Custer

254
00:11:51,410 --> 00:11:53,750
have followed the tweets of Sitting Bull?

255
00:11:53,750 --> 00:11:56,150
Would not Lee have followed Grant?

256
00:11:56,150 --> 00:11:58,720
Would not Spy have followed Spy?

257
00:12:00,190 --> 00:12:02,420
I have more examples, but excuse me.

258
00:12:02,420 --> 00:12:04,090
Hello.

259
00:12:04,090 --> 00:12:06,520
Well, this seems like an odd time

260
00:12:06,530 --> 00:12:09,990
to test my cell phone quality, but go on.

261
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,260
Test phrases? All right.

262
00:12:13,270 --> 00:12:15,230
Im a tote.

263
00:12:15,230 --> 00:12:17,270
Ulba.

264
00:12:17,270 --> 00:12:18,840
Twad.

